From 8ffd7bfcceb05306da65f5f2c27eab4d6bd81d7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:46:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add SegmentedControl
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A radio group styled as a segmented track — for switching how the same
content is shown (List / Board / Calendar), not for moving between
different content.

Ported from the Claude Design export and retokenised: the export carried
raw rgb() values and CSS-variable fallbacks, this version uses semantic
tokens only, so dark theme works without a second code path. No new
tokens were needed.

Two changes from the export, both deliberate:

- Sizes are 32 / 40px (sm / md) rather than 28 / 36, matching Button's
  scale so 'size' means the same thing on every control, and so md meets
  the 40px minimum target in CLAUDE.md.
- Keyboard support added. The export was mouse-only: it had the radiogroup
  roles but no arrow-key movement and no managed tab order. The whole
  control is now one tab stop with arrow keys moving between segments.

Known softness, documented in docs/segmented-control.md: the selected
segment's white surface sits at 1.1:1 against the track, so the selected
state leans on the label's colour and weight change to satisfy WCAG 1.4.11.
Making the surface itself clear 3:1 would need a new token.
